# Nook server settings. The installer writes this for you:
#
#   curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nebbsie/stream/main/server/install.sh | sh
#
# Only the domain has to be set. Everything else has a default; take the # off
# a line to change it, then run: docker compose up -d

# The name this server answers on. Point its DNS at this machine first.
CATHODE_DOMAIN=cathode.example.org

# Made by the installer. Any long random string: openssl rand -hex 32
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
CATHODE_TURN_SECRET=

# Which extras to start: tls for HTTPS (Caddy), turn for calls (coturn).
# Leave out tls if you already have a proxy in front, and set CATHODE_BIND=0.0.0.0.
COMPOSE_PROFILES=tls,turn

# --- everything below is optional ---------------------------------------

# The pages that may use this server, comma separated. * is any page.
# CATHODE_ORIGINS=*

# This server's own address. Default: https:// and the domain.
# CATHODE_PUBLIC_URL=https://cathode.example.org

# 0 lets a call try a direct path before the TURN relay.
# CATHODE_TURN_ONLY=1

# A cluster with friends: their servers, and one secret you all share.
# CATHODE_PEERS=https://friend-one.example.org,https://friend-two.example.org
# CATHODE_CLUSTER_SECRET=

# Files: the largest one may be, and how much one space may keep, in bytes.
# CATHODE_MAX_FILE_BYTES=104857600
# CATHODE_MAX_ROOM_FILE_BYTES=5368709120

# GIF search, for everybody in the spaces on this server. One key is enough,
# from whichever service you like; the first one set here is used.
#   Klipy: a test key in a minute, https://partner.klipy.com/api-keys
#   Tenor: a Google API key, https://developers.google.com/tenor
#   Giphy: after registering an app, https://developers.giphy.com
# CATHODE_KLIPY_KEY=
# CATHODE_TENOR_KEY=
# CATHODE_GIPHY_KEY=
